(1435,3011,'Difficult childbirth or labor.','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:39',NULL,NULL,'3497FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1436,3012,'A transient loss of consciousness and postural tone caused by diminished blood flow to the brain (i.e., BRAIN ISCHEMIA). Presyncope refers to the sensation of lightheadedness and loss of strength that precedes a syncopal event or accompanies an incomplete syncope. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp367-9)','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:40',NULL,NULL,'3485FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1437,3013,'Conditions characterized by disturbances of usual sleep patterns or behaviors. Sleep disorders may be divided into three major categories: DYSSOMNIAS (i.e. disorders characterized by insomnia or hypersomnia), PARASOMNIAS (abnormal sleep behaviors), and sleep disorders secondary to medical or psychiatric disorders. (From Thorpy, Sleep Disorders Medicine, 1994, p187)','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:40',NULL,NULL,'3474FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1438,3015,'An unpleasant sensation induced by noxious stimuli and generally received by specialized nerve endings.','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:40',NULL,NULL,'15592FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1439,3019,'A cognitive disorder characterized by an impaired ability to comprehend written and printed words or phrases despite intact vision. This condition may be developmental or acquired. Developmental dyslexia is marked by reading achievement that falls substantially below that expected given the individual&#39;s chronological age, measured intelligence, and age-appropriate education. The disturbance in reading significantly interferes with academic achievement or with activities of daily living that require reading skills. (From DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:41',NULL,NULL,'3450FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1440,3022,'A type of acneiform disorder in which secondary pyogenic infection in and around pilosebaceous structures ends in keloidal scarring. It manifests as persistent folliculitis of the back of the neck associated with occlusion of the follicular orifices. It is most often encountered in black or Asian men.','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:41',NULL,NULL,'15583FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1441,3023,'A chronic disorder of the pilosebaceous apparatus associated with an increase in sebum secretion. It is characterized by open comedones (blackheads), closed comedones (whiteheads), and pustular nodules. The cause is unknown, but heredity and age are predisposing factors.','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:41',NULL,NULL,'15578FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1442,3025,'Harm or hurt to the ankle or ankle joint usually inflicted by an external source.','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:41',NULL,NULL,'3430FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1443,3028,'A collective term for muscle and ligament injuries without dislocation or fracture. A sprain is a joint injury in which some of the fibers of a supporting ligament are ruptured but the continuity of the ligament remains intact. A strain is an overstretching or overexertion of some part of the musculature.','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:41',NULL,NULL,'3426FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1444,3030,'A disease of infants due to group 2 phage type 17 staphylococci that produce an epidermolytic exotoxin. Superficial fine vesicles and bullae form and rupture easily, resulting in loss of large sheets of epidermis.','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:41',NULL,NULL,'3417FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1445,3032,'Skin diseases characterized by local or general distributions of blisters. They are classified according to the site and mode of blister formation. Lesions can appear spontaneously or be precipitated by infection, trauma, or sunlight. Etiologies include immunologic and genetic factors. (From Scientific American Medicine, 1990)','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:41',NULL,NULL,'3378FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1446,3034,'Disorders related to substance abuse, the side effects of a medication, toxin exposure, and alcohol related disorders','en',2,'2026-05-31 02:13:42',NULL,NULL,'3374FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
